From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: retain live O82 timing when a modeset disables AVR

KWin 6.8 can test a refresh change with VRR enabled, then disable VRR in
the real modeset and enable it again on presentation. Requiring identical
VRR state excludes that real commit and resets the panel and touch RAM.

Admit the disable transition when the old AVR session is healthy. Existing
prepare-for-kickoff processing disables both INTFs and DSI QSync before the
common timing flush. No new enable operation is needed while DSI shadow
timing is pending. Retain the full modeset for simultaneous VRR entry from
fixed timing, and preserve all active, connector, color and paired guards.

Signed-off-by: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_atomic.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_atomic.c
@@ -210,7 +210,7 @@
 
 	for_each_oldnew_crtc_in_state(state, crtc, old, new, i) {
 		if (!old->active || !new->active || !new->mode_changed ||
-		    old->vrr_enabled != new->vrr_enabled ||
+		    (!old->vrr_enabled && new->vrr_enabled) ||
 		    new->active_changed || new->connectors_changed ||
 		    new->color_mgmt_changed || old->encoder_mask != new->encoder_mask ||
 		    hweight32(new->encoder_mask) != 1)
